{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"fb36f631-80e4-476a-b4f7-d6d309a7171e","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Summary of Findings \u0026 Fix\n\nDuring the authorization audit across all endpoints, an **Object-Level Authorization (IDOR / BOLA)** vulnerability was identified and fixed:\n\n1. **Vulnerability Identified**:\n   - `POST /tasks/{id}/like` and `POST /tasks/{id}/view` lacked the `can_access(user, task)` authorization guard.\n   - When Account B (Bob) probed Account A's (Alice) private task `#1`, all standard endpoints (`GET`, `PATCH`, `DELETE`, `comments`, `complete`, `nudge`) correctly returned `403 Forbidden`.\n   - However, `POST /tasks/1/like` and `POST /tasks/1/view` returned `200 OK` and mutated Alice's private task attributes (`likes` and `views`).\n\n2. **Fix Implemented in [`api.py`](file:///tmp/h-ia3MHG/api.py#L163-L172)**:\n   - Added `if not can_access(user, task): return self.send(403, {\"error\": \"forbidden\"})` checks to both `like` and `view` actions.\n\n3. **Regression Tests Added in [`tests/test_api.py`](file:///tmp/h-ia3MHG/tests/test_api.py#L71-L101)**:\n   - Added tests ensuring that any attempt by a non-owner to interact with a private task via any endpoint returns `403 Forbidden` and does not mutate task state.\n   - Verified that the owner can still view and like their own private tasks.\n   - All 7 tests in the suite pass.\n\n4. **Report**:\n   - Detailed findings, evidence matrix, and remediation notes have been written to [`ANSWER.md`](file:///tmp/h-ia3MHG/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":96.632177,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":147930,"output_tokens":7023,"thinking_tokens":3260,"cache_read_tokens":210925,"total_tokens":154953}}}
